  "question": {
    "text": "Assuming that water vapour is an ideal gas, the internal energy $(\\Delta \\mathrm{U})$ when $1\\mathrm{~mol}$ of water is vapourised at $1 \\mathrm{~bar}$ pressure and $100^{\\circ} \\mathrm{C}$, (Given: Molar enthalpy of vapourization of water at $1 \\mathrm{~bar}$ and $373 \\mathrm{~K}=41 \\mathrm{~kJ} \\mathrm{~mol}^{-1}$ and $\\mathrm{R}=8.3 \\mathrm{~J} \\mathrm{~mol}^{-1} \\mathrm{~K}^{-1}$ ) will be"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "\n$4.100 \\mathrm{~kJ} \\mathrm{~mol}^{-1}$\n",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "\n$3.7904 \\mathrm{~kJ} \\mathrm{~mol}^{-1}$\n",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "\n$37.904 \\mathrm{~kJ} \\mathrm{~mol}^{-1}$\n",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "\n$41.00 \\mathrm{~kJ} \\mathrm{~mol}^{-1}$",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "C"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "$\\begin{aligned}\n& \\mathrm{H}_2 \\mathrm{O}(\\ell) \\stackrel{\\text { vaporisation }}{\\longrightarrow} \\mathrm{H}_2 \\mathrm{O}(\\mathrm{g}) \\\\\n& \\Delta \\mathrm{n}_{\\mathrm{g}}=1-0=1 \\\\\n& \\Delta \\mathrm{H}=\\Delta \\mathrm{U}+\\Delta \\mathrm{n}_{\\mathrm{g}} \\mathrm{RT} \\\\\n& \\Delta \\mathrm{U}=\\Delta \\mathrm{H}-\\Delta \\mathrm{n}_{\\mathrm{g}} \\mathrm{RT} \\\\\n& =41-8.3 \\times 10^{-3} \\times 373 \\\\\n& =37.9 \\mathrm{~kJ} \\mathrm{~mol}^{-1}\n\\end{aligned}$\nHence, (C) is correct."
  }
}